        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">The ambient pressure on an object is the pressure of the surrounding medium, such as a gas or liquid,
    which comes into contact with the object. The SI unit of pressure is the pascal (Pa), which is a very small unit relative to
    atmospheric pressure on Earth, so kilopascals ($kPa$) are more commonly used in this context.
  </dcterms:description>
