        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">The pressure exerted by the weight of the air above it at any point on the earth&apos;s surface. At sea level
    the atmosphere will support a column of mercury about $760 mm$ high. This decreases with increasing altitude. The standard
    value for the atmospheric pressure at sea level in SI units is $101,325 pascals$.
  </dcterms:description>
        <qudt:informativeReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/acref/acref-9780199233991</qudt:informativeReference>
