        <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificVolume"/>
        <qudt:plainTextDescription>In the context of a chemical durability test, this is measure of how much of a solution (often a
    corrosive or reactive one) is consumed or used up per unit mass of a material being tested. In other words, this the volume of
    solution needed to cause a certain level of chemical reaction or damage to a given mass of the material.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
        <rdfs:comment>Applicable units are those of quantitykind:SpecificVolume</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chemical Consumption per Mass</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


