        <qudt:plainTextDescription>The pressure of blood in the arteries which rises to a maximum as blood is pumped out by the left
    ventricle (systole) and drops to a minimum in diastole. The systolic/diastolic pressure is normally ~120/80 mmHg in a young
    adult.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
