        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">&quot;Gap Energy&quot; is the difference in energy between the lowest level of conduction band and the highest
    level of valence band. It is an energy range in a solid where no electron states can exist.
  </dcterms:description>
        <qudt:informativeReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Band_gap</qudt:informativeReference>
        <qudt:plainTextDescription>&quot;Gap Energy&quot; is the difference in energy between the lowest level of conduction band and the
    highest level of valence band. It is an energy range in a solid where no electron states can exist.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
        <qudt:symbol>E_g</qudt:symbol>
        <rdfs:comment>Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
