        <qudt:latexDefinition rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">$r = \frac{d}{2}$, where $d$ is the circle diameter.</qudt:latexDefinition>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">In classical geometry, the &quot;Radius&quot; of a circle or sphere is any line segment from its center to its
