        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">The solid angle subtended by a surface S is defined as the surface area of a unit sphere covered by the
    surface S&apos;s projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary angle
    is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of solid
    angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi.
  </dcterms:description>
