    the surface S&apos;s projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary
    angle is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of
    solid angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
