        <qudt:latexDefinition rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">$L_P = 10 \log_{10} \frac{p^2}{p_0^2} dB$, where $p$ is sound pressure and the reference value in airborne acoustics is $p_0 = 20 \mu Pa$.</qudt:latexDefinition>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">Sound pressure level ($SPL$) or sound level is a logarithmic measure of the effective sound pressure of a
    sound relative to a reference value. It is measured in decibels (dB) above a standard reference level.
  </dcterms:description>
        <qudt:informativeReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_pressure#Sound_pressure_level</qudt:informativeReference>
