        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-FT2"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-IN2"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-M2"/>
        <qudt:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/EnergyFluenceRate"/>
        <qudt:hasDimensionVector rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T-3D0"/>
        <qudt:specializationOf rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PowerPerArea"/>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PowerPerArea"/>
        <qudt:eclassCode>0173-1#Z4-BAJ318#004</qudt:eclassCode>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">ratio between the differential change in the energy fluence dΨ and the time interval dt: ψ = dΨ / dt; the
    total radiance is identical to the product of the particle flux density and the average energy of the particles
  </dcterms:description>
        <qudt:plainTextDescription xml:lang="de">Quotient aus der differentiellen Änderung der Energiefluenz dΨ im Zeitintervall dt: ψ = dΨ / dt;
    die Energieflussdichte ist identisch mit dem Produkt der Teilchenflussdichte und der mittleren Teilchenenergie
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
        <rdfs:comment>Applicable units are those of quantitykind:PowerPerArea</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en-us">Total Radiance</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/TouchThresholds -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/TouchThresholds">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"/>
        <qudt:hasDimensionVector rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/NotApplicable"/>
        <qudt:isoNormativeReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=43012</qudt:isoNormativeReference>
        <qudt:latexSymbol rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">$\overline{T_t}$</qudt:latexSymbol>
        <dcterms:description>&quot;Touch Thresholds&quot; is an umbrella term for the thresholds of sensitivity of the skin to touch, vibration
    and other mechanical stimuli. It has no single dimension: a concrete touch threshold specializes into a force for light-touch
    detection (e.g. von Frey monofilaments, in millinewtons), a length for vibration-detection amplitude or two-point separation,
    or a pressure, depending on the stimulus and method.
  </dcterms:description>
        <qudt:plainTextDescription>&quot;Touch Thresholds&quot; is an umbrella term for the thresholds of sensitivity of the skin to touch,
    vibration and other mechanical stimuli. It has no single dimension: a concrete touch threshold specializes into a force for
    light-touch detection (e.g. von Frey monofilaments, in millinewtons), a length for vibration-detection amplitude or two-point
    separation, or a pressure, depending on the stimulus and method.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Touch Thresholds</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ToxicEquivalent -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ToxicEquivalent">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoGM"/>
        <qudt:hasDimensionVector rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T0D0"/>
        <qudt:organizedUnder rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassEquivalent"/>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassEquivalent"/>
        <dcterms:description>The toxic equivalent (TEQ) expresses the toxicity of a mixture of dioxin-like compounds (polychlorinated dibenzodioxins, dibenzofurans and biphenyls) as the mass of the most toxic congener, 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin (TCDD), that would have the same toxicity. It is the sum over the congeners of each congener&apos;s mass multiplied by its toxic equivalency factor (TEF). The value therefore depends on the TEF scheme used (for example WHO 2005 or I-TEF), which should be stated with the quantity. TEQ values are expressed in ordinary mass units, such as ng or pg; the TEF belongs to the quantity, not to the unit, so Toxic Equivalent is organized under Mass Equivalent without being asserted commensurable with plain mass.</dcterms:description>
        <qudt:informativeReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toxic_equivalency_factor</qudt:informativeReference>
        <rdfs:comment>Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ToxicEquivalent</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Toxic Equivalent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ToxicEquivalentFlowRate -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ToxicEquivalentFlowRate">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"/>
        <qudt:applicableUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-YR"/>
        <qudt:hasDimensionVector rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T-1D0"/>
        <qudt:organizedUnder rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassFlowRate"/>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassFlowRate"/>
        <dcterms:description>The toxic equivalent flow rate is the toxic equivalent (TEQ) of dioxin-like compounds released or transferred per unit time, for example the annual TEQ emission of an installation to air. As with Toxic Equivalent, the value depends on the toxic equivalency factor (TEF) scheme used, which should be stated with the quantity. Values are expressed in ordinary mass flow rate units, such as g/a; the TEF belongs to the quantity, not to the unit, so Toxic Equivalent Flow Rate is organized under Mass Flow Rate without being asserted commensurable with it.</dcterms:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ToxicEquivalentFlowRate</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Toxic Equivalent Flow Rate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


