        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">
The $\textit{International Unit per Milliliter}$ is a unit for  &apos;Serum Or Plasma Level&apos; expressed as $IU/mL$.
The magnitude of one $IU/L$ depends on the material, so there is no single conversion multiplier.
Following the mass-equivalent treatment of $IU$ (see unit:IU), this is dimensioned as a mass concentration.
</dcterms:description>
        <qudt:expression rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">$IU/mL$</qudt:expression>
        <qudt:symbol>IU/mL</qudt:symbol>
