    imperial and U.S. customary systems. The most commonly used acres today are the international acre and, in the United States,
    the survey acre. The most common use of the acre is to measure tracts of land. One international acre is equal to 4046.8564224
    square metres.
  </qudt:plainTextDescription>
        <qudt:symbol>lbm/acre</qudt:symbol>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pound Mass per Acre</rdfs:label>
