        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">The $\textit{ohm}$ is the SI derived unit of electrical resistance, named after German physicist Georg
    Simon Ohm.  It is defined as:  $$\Omega \equiv\ \frac{\text{V}}{\text{A}}\ \equiv\
    \frac{\text{volt}}{\text{amp}}\ \equiv\ \frac{\text{W}}{\text {A}^{2}}\ \equiv\
