        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">A petabyte is a unit of information equal to one quadrillion bytes, or 1024 terabytes. The unit symbol
    for the petabyte is PB. The prefix peta (P) indicates the fifth power to 1000: 1 PB = 1000000000000000B, 1 million gigabytes =
