        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;p&gt;The short ton is a unit of mass equal to 2,000 pounds (907.18474 kg). In the United States it is often
    called simply ton without distinguishing it from the metric ton (tonne, 1,000 kilograms / 2,204.62262 pounds) or the long ton
    (2,240 pounds / 1,016.0469088 kilograms); rather, the other two are specifically noted. There are, however, some U.S.
    applications for which unspecified tons normally means long tons.&lt;/p&gt;
  </dcterms:description>
