        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&apos;Volt per Second&apos; is a unit of magnetic flux equaling one weber. This is the flux passing through a
    conducting loop and reduced to zero at a uniform rate in one second inducing an electric potential of one volt in the loop.
  </dcterms:description>
