        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString">The unit $\textit{Watt Per Square Meter Kelvin }$ ($W m^{-2} K^{-1}$) is a unit in the category of
    Thermal heat transfer coefficient. It is also known as $\textit{watt/square meter-kelvin}$. This unit is commonly used in the
