        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">A yard is a unit of length in several different systems including United States customary units, Imperial
    units and the former English units. It is equal to 3 feet or 36 inches. Under an agreement in 1959 between Australia, Canada,
    New Zealand, South Africa, the United Kingdom and the United States, the yard (known as the &quot;international yard&quot; in the United
    States) was legally defined to be exactly 0.9144 metres.
  </dcterms:description>
